SmartSessionLens::setConfig
├── given valid configuration and enable data
│   ├── when caller is the account
│   │   ├── it should emit SmartSessionEmissaryConfigUpdated event
│   │   ├── it should enable the permission
│   │   ├── it should derive correct lockTag from allocator, scope, and resetPeriod
│   │   ├── it should increment nonce for replay protection
│   │   └── it should not require user signature
│   └── when caller is not the account
│       ├── given valid user signature
│       │   └── it should enable the permission
│       └── given invalid user signature
│           └── it should revert with InvalidUserSignature
├── given session with policies
│   ├── when session has claim policies
│   │   └── it should enable claim policies for the lockTag
│   ├── when session has ERC7739 policies
│   │   └── it should enable ERC1271 policies
│   ├── when session has action policies
│   │   └── it should enable action policies with correct actionId
│   ├── when session has multiple actions
│   │   └── it should enable all actions
│   └── when session has multiple policies per action
│       └── it should enable all policies for the action
├── given different scope values
│   ├── when scope is ChainSpecific
│   │   └── it should derive lockTag with ChainSpecific scope
│   └── when scope is Multichain
│       └── it should derive lockTag with Multichain scope
├── given different resetPeriod values
│   ├── when resetPeriod is OneSecond
│   │   └── it should derive lockTag with OneSecond resetPeriod
│   └── when resetPeriod is OneMinute
│       └── it should derive lockTag with OneMinute resetPeriod
├── given NO_LOCKTAG (allocator is address(0))
│   ├── when called on init
│   │   └── it should not require allocator signature
│   ├── when called on subsequent calls
│   │   └── it should not require allocator signature
│   └── it should skip claim policy enablement but still enable action policies
├── given multiple lockTags for same permissionId
│   └── it should enable both lockTags independently
├── given different allocators
│   └── it should derive unique lockTags per allocator
├── given lockTag isolation
│   ├── when same lockTag used by different permissionIds
│   │   └── it should isolate lockTags per permissionId
│   └── when same permissionId and lockTag but different accounts
│       └── it should isolate lockTags per account
├── given init vs subsequent calls
│   ├── when lockTag is not yet enabled (init)
│   │   ├── it should not require allocator signature
│   │   └── it should add lockTag to enabledLockTags for this permissionId
│   └── when lockTag is already enabled (subsequent)
│       ├── given valid allocator signature
│       │   └── it should succeed
│       └── given invalid allocator signature
│           └── it should revert with InvalidAllocatorSignature
├── given nonce management
│   └── it should track nonces independently per lockTag
├── given session validator
│   ├── when called on init
│   │   └── it should set session validator and config
│   └── when called on subsequent calls
│       └── it should not change existing validator
├── given multichain enable data
│   ├── when chainDigestIndex points to current chain
│   │   └── it should succeed
│   ├── when chainDigestIndex points to wrong chain
│   │   └── it should revert with ChainIdMismatch
│   ├── when session digest doesn't match computed digest
│   │   └── it should revert with HashMismatch
│   ├── when single chain in multichain array
│   │   └── it should succeed
│   └── when different digests per chain
│       └── it should validate only current chain's digest
└── given invalid enable data
    ├── when expires is in the past
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidEmissaryEnableData
    ├── when expires equals current timestamp
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidEmissaryEnableData
    ├── when permissionId doesn't match session
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPermissionId
    └── when nonce has already been used (replay)
        └── it should revert with HashMismatch